title: 'T-006 shipped — atelier transcribe + transcript edit family + captions regenerate'
summary: 'Implemented T-006 (Whisper transcribe + editable captions) end-to-end same day as T-007b. Three commits, no new npm dependencies, 32 new tests added (97/97 in CLI, 560/560 across the workspace — all green). The pipeline: probeWhisper (whisper-cpp / openai-api / none) → runWhisperCpp via child_process.spawn → parseWhisperCppJson (token-level timing when available, even-split fallback) → mergeTranscriptWithExisting (preserves userEdited/userAdded/hidden flags on words matching by start time ±0.3s AND unchanged detected text, re-inserts userAdded orphans by timing) → writeTranscript 1.1 → rewriteCaptionLayers (drops only caption-tagged layers + their deltas from the default state, preserves everything else). Six CLI commands total: atelier transcribe, atelier transcript fix/add/delete/merge/split/list, atelier captions regenerate. All edit commands set the appropriate flag (userEdited/userAdded/hidden) and trigger caption regeneration unless --no-regenerate. The layer-tag isolation invariant now proven across BOTH pipelines (silence-trim and caption) by test — re-running either never destroys the other''s output or any user-authored layers. The detected-vs-user-edited convention is now firmly established as Atelier''s architecture for any AI-generated content that the user will need to tweak.'
