  - 50525a8  # whisper + transcript-model + caption-builder pure libs (core)
  - a87919f  # transcribe + transcript + captions commands + docs + versions (surface)
learnings:
  - 'The three-layer build pattern (foundation → core → surface) used for T-007b worked equally well for T-006. Same three commits, same independence — no commit needed amending. Codify this as the team''s ship-pattern for medium-sized features.'
  - 'mergeTranscriptWithExisting''s match rule (start_time within 0.3s AND detected text unchanged) is correct. If detected text changes, we drop the user override — otherwise a re-transcribe could silently mis-attribute a fix from one word to a different one Whisper now hears in that slot. Test "does not preserve override when detected text changes" guards this.'
  - 'userAdded orphan preservation requires a separate pass — these words have no matching fresh detection by definition. Insert by timing into whichever segment contains that timestamp. Tested.'
  - 'rewriteCaptionLayers writes caption deltas into the default state if it exists, else the first state. Caption regeneration is idempotent — running it twice replaces, never appends. This invariant tested twice (once each in T-007b for cuts and T-006 for captions).'
  - 'whisper.cpp emits special tokens like [_BEG_] in the token list that must be filtered out before treating them as words. Parser does this; tested explicitly.'
  - 'parseWhisperCppJson falls back to even-split word timing when only segment-level offsets are present (i.e., when --output-json is used instead of --output-json-full). For T-006 v1 this is acceptable — token-level offsets give precise word timing, even-split gives a usable approximation when not.'
  - 'The CLI surface deliberately keeps `transcript` as a subcommand family (fix/add/delete/merge/split/list) rather than flat commands. This mirrors `git`-style ergonomics and leaves room for future verbs without polluting the top-level namespace.'
  - 'Studio package accumulating pre-existing typecheck errors (Shape narrowing in property-panel, six unused-var/imports in controls and test). All confirmed unrelated to T-006 by inspection — only types/cli touched. Should be its own audit pass. The fact that pnpm -r test still passes 560/560 means runtime behavior is unaffected; this is type-level drift that wants cleanup, not bugs.'
